-- title:
--   Reduced generic fibre of the H₁ moduli ring, with its rank
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $K$ an $A$-algebra over $L$, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is that of the modular invariant, assumed nonzero. Assume $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$; assume the variable-change compatibilities for $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points, for the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel polynomial conditions, and for divisibility of `inLineMulPoly`; let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras with invertible discriminant which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity, and $\mathcal T$ a level transport for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ which is a section transport; assume the graded realisability of variable changes and of coefficient homomorphisms on projective models (hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO`). Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package over $A$ for the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — a ring $B_0$ of finite type over $A$ with a universal point representing the functor — and let $x$ be a point of that datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant expands to `jqNModC L q`. Writing $S=A[P_0.j_0]\subseteq B_0$, assumed a domain, and $F=\operatorname{Frac}S$, the conclusion is that $F\otimes_S B_0$ is reduced and $$\dim_F(F\otimes_S B_0)=\Big(\prod_{p\mid M'}p^{v_p(M')-1}(p+1)\Big)(\ell_g-1)\,\lvert\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)\rvert/2,$$ the division by $2$ being division of natural numbers.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre statement for the fine moduli ring of the combined level structure ($\Gamma_0$-type kernel data at the primes of $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point linked to them, and a Drinfeld basis at $q$): over the fraction field of the subring generated by the $j$-invariant of the universal object, the moduli ring is reduced of dimension $\psi(M')(\ell_g-1)\lvert\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb F_q)\rvert/2$. It feeds the determination of the minimal primes of the moduli ring and the identification of its components with the modular curve of level $H_1$.
